# NOTE: a blanket `/blog/*  /blog/post  200` rewrite used to live here as a fallback for posts
# not yet baked into a static directory. Removed — Cloudflare Pages evaluates _redirects BEFORE
# static asset resolution, not after, so that rule was shadowing every real generated post
# (old and new) behind the generic client-rendered shell, including for search crawlers and link
# previews that don't run JS. The client-rendered fallback for a genuinely-missing post (weekly
# cron published since the last rebuild) now lives at public/blog/404.html instead, which
# Cloudflare Pages serves natively as the nearest-directory 404 page — a real 404 status for
# search engines, still a working page for a human who clicked a fresh link.

